<section class="page-hero">
  <div class="wrap">
    <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / Free local SEO audit</nav>
    <h1>Can local customers find your business online?</h1>
    <p class="lede">A free, manually reviewed look at your Google Business Profile, reviews and local search visibility — so you know exactly what's holding you back from showing up first.</p>
    <div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn--primary" href="#seo-form" data-track-cta="local_seo_audit">Get my free local visibility report</a></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--mist" aria-labelledby="what-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2 id="what-h">What local SEO actually means</h2>
      <p class="lede">When someone searches "roofer near me" or "kitchen renovation Whitby," Google decides which businesses to show using three main signals: your Google Business Profile, how consistent your business information is across the web, and how relevant your website is to that search. Local SEO is the ongoing work of strengthening all three.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="problems-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2 id="problems-h">Common local visibility problems</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="rows">
      <div class="row"><h3>No claimed, optimized Google Business Profile</h3><p>Or one that's claimed but incomplete — missing categories, hours, services or photos.</p></div>
      <div class="row"><h3>Inconsistent business information</h3><p>Different phone numbers, addresses or business names across your website, Google and other listings confuses both customers and Google.</p></div>
      <div class="row"><h3>Few or no reviews</h3><p>Review count and recency are a major factor in who Google shows first in the map pack.</p></div>
      <div class="row"><h3>No local landing pages</h3><p>A single generic page can't rank for every city and service you offer.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--mist" aria-labelledby="scorecard-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2 id="scorecard-h">What your visibility report covers</h2>
      <p class="lede">We review each of these by hand and note what's strong, what's missing and what to fix first. Local results vary by location, device and the exact search used, so we report gaps and opportunities, not a guaranteed ranking.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="rows">
      <div class="row"><h3>Google Business Profile completeness</h3><p>Categories, hours, services, photos and description.</p></div>
      <div class="row"><h3>Business description</h3><p>Whether it clearly says what you do and where you work.</p></div>
      <div class="row"><h3>Website local relevance</h3><p>Whether your website names your services and service area clearly.</p></div>
      <div class="row"><h3>Review profile</h3><p>Count, recency and whether you're responding to reviews.</p></div>
      <div class="row"><h3>Local landing pages</h3><p>Whether you have a dedicated page per city and service, or one page trying to rank for everything.</p></div>
      <div class="row"><h3>Business information consistency</h3><p>Whether your name, address and phone number match across your website and Google.</p></div>
      <div class="row"><h3>Directory visibility</h3><p>A general sense of where else your business does or doesn't appear — see our <a href="/directory-scan/">full directory visibility scan</a> for a dedicated check.</p></div>
      <div class="row"><h3>Local keyword opportunities</h3><p>Searches real people in your area likely use that your site isn't currently targeting.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="benefits-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2 id="benefits-h">Why this is worth fixing</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="rows">
      <div class="row"><h3>Google Business Profile optimization</h3><p>Often the first thing a potential customer sees, before they ever visit your website.</p></div>
      <div class="row"><h3>Directory and citation consistency</h3><p>Matching business information across directories is one of the signals Google uses to trust your location and category.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

